# No configurator commits / no companion-app PRs to ATOV

Never `git add`, commit, or push anything under `configurator/`.

- Firmware, docs/cheatsheet are fine when asked.
- Local configurator edits for testing are OK; leave them unstaged or discard before commit.
- If a commit accidentally includes `configurator/`, stop and unstage/restore those paths before committing.

## Companion webapps (Presetpunk / Scopepunk)

**Presetpunk** (`faderpunk-preset-editor/` / brand **Presetpunk**) and **Scopepunk**
(`faderpunk-diagnostics/`) are personal tools. They must **not** be opened as PRs
against `github.com/ATOVproject/faderpunk`.

Canonical home: https://github.com/kosmar/faderpunk-tools  
(also fine on branches of https://github.com/kosmar/faderpunk).

When asked to commit/push these apps, push to `kosmar/faderpunk-tools` (or the
`kosmar/faderpunk` fork) — never open a PR to ATOV for them.

## Existing app PRs

WIP **firmware/configurator** apps already have open PRs. Before opening a new PR,
check the list and push to the matching feature branch instead:

https://github.com/ATOVproject/faderpunk/pulls
